  "comment": "**What it does**\nThe **O'Shaughnessy small-cap combo** - cheap on sales AND already winning. One of the best long-run track records among the classic screens.\n\n- **Small** - $300M to $2B.\n- **Cheap on sales** - price-to-sales below its industry median. Sales-based on purpose: small companies often are not profitable yet, and that is fine here.\n- **Already winning** - RS Rank 70+ and revenue growing (3-year, falling back to 1-year).\n- **Tradeable** - 100k average daily volume, so you can actually get in and out of a small cap.\n\n**Your choices baked in**: volatility expected - dividends ignored - normal stocks only.\n\n**How to tweak**\n- **Want a tighter shortlist?** Raise `rs_rank` to 80 - that is the block doing the heavy cutting (535 to 176).\n- **Want deeper value?** P/S vs industry is a relative test. Add a raw `ps < 1` block for absolute cheapness too.\n- **Want micro caps?** Lower the floor to $100M, but tighten `vol_20d_avg` or you will surface names you cannot trade.\n- **Want profitable names only?** Add `net_margin > 0` - but that removes the point of using sales rather than earnings.\n\n**How to sort for best picks**\n- **Sort by `momentum_score`** - the 'already winning' half of the thesis.\n- **Tiebreak on `growth_score`** - revenue growth behind the price move.\n- **Avoid `quality_score`** - small caps score poorly on quality by nature, so it would just rank them by size and maturity.\n- **Careful with `value_score`** - it leans on earnings multiples that many of these names do not have.",
  "ai_instructions": "Find small companies that are cheap on sales AND already winning \u2014 the\nO'Shaughnessy small-cap growth & value combo (the best long-run track record of\nthe classic screens).\n- **Goal**: growth + value combo. **Dividends**: ignore.\n- **Size**: small caps, roughly $300M-$2B.\n- **Cheap on sales**: price-to-sales below its industry (sales-based on purpose \u2014\n  small companies often aren't profitable yet, and that is FINE here).\n- **Already winning**: strong recent price strength (RS Rank 70+), revenue growing.\n- **Tradeable**: enough daily volume to get in and out.\n- **Risk**: volatile is expected. **Kinds**: normal stocks only.\n- **Results**: ~50-200 names. **Sorting**: momentum first, tiebreak growth.",
